        "text": "{\"supportingParagraphIds\":[\"p0075\",\"p0038\",\"p0079\"],\"proposal\":{\"ops\":[{\"kind\":\"insert_after\",\"paragraphId\":\"p0075\",\"text\":\"INDEMNIFICATION. Vendor shall defend and indemnify Customer and its Affiliates from and against any third-party claim, and all resulting damages, costs and expenses (including reasonable attorneys' fees), to the extent arising out of (a) an allegation that the Services or Deliverables infringe or misappropriate any intellectual property right; (b) Vendor's breach of Applicable Law; (c) any unauthorized access to or disclosure of Customer Data caused by Vendor; or (d) Vendor's gross negligence or wilful misconduct. The indemnified Party shall give the indemnifying Party prompt written notice of the claim, the indemnifying Party shall control the defence of the claim, and the indemnified Party shall provide reasonable cooperation. Customer shall indemnify Vendor from and against any third-party claim to the extent arising out of content or materials provided by Customer for use in the Services or Customer's breach of Applicable Law.\",\"numbering\":\"20\",\"asHeading\":false}],\"comment\":\"[Playbook] No indemnification article exists, so we have inserted one concise Section 20 in which Vendor defends and indemnifies Customer and its Affiliates for third-party IP infringement, breach of Applicable Law, Vendor-caused Customer Data breaches and gross negligence or wilful misconduct, with a notice/control/cooperation procedure and Customer's indemnity confined to Customer-provided content and Customer's breach of Applicable Law. This is our preferred position; we have dropped hold-harmless, settlement and remedy extras to keep the addition minimal.\",\"level\":\"preferred\",\"summary\":\"Insert a single concise Section 20 Vendor defence and indemnity (IP, breach of law, Vendor-caused data breach, gross negligence/wilful misconduct) with notice/control/cooperation procedure and a narrow Customer indemnity.\"},\